simplePage("newsletter/index.html","THE CIVORA DIGEST","The Newsletter","A deliberate weekly selection of the stories worth your attention.",`<div class="newsletter-panel"><span class="newsletter-big">THE WEEK, IN CONTEXT.</span><h2>Coming soon.</h2><p>Our email newsletter hasn't launched. We're not collecting addresses or pretending to have an active mailing list. When it does launch, subscriptions will be opt-in and clearly described.</p></div><h2>What we're planning</h2><p>A short editorial note, important explainers, links to primary evidence, and a thoughtful reading list—with no fake urgency or clickbait.</p>`,"newsletter");
simplePage("about/index.html","OUR PUBLICATION","About Civora","Independent by design. Interested in substance over noise.",`<h2>What Civora is</h2><p>Civora News is an independent digital publication covering U.S. affairs, world developments, technology, business, science and culture through source-based reports, original explainers and careful attribution.</p><p>The initial published edition draws from publicly available materials of agencies and scientific organizations. These articles were researched and drafted with AI assistance; their primary sources are linked for readers to inspect. We do not claim original interviews, field reporting or scientific measurements that were not conducted.</p><h2>Our commitments</h2><p>Accuracy before speed. Clear separation of news, opinion and advertising. Honest corrections. Respect for source material and original reporting. No invented quotes or staged reporting presented as fact.</p><h2>Who runs it?</h2><p>The publication is currently an independent project. A public masthead and newsroom contact will be added as appropriate before commissioning outside reporting.</p>`,"about");
simplePage("standards/index.html","HOW WE WORK","Editorial Standards","The audience deserves verifiable information, clear attribution and visible corrections.",`<h2>Evidence comes before a headline</h2><p>We check dates, units, definitions, denominators, publication context and named sources before presenting a finding as fact. Whenever possible, we link primary documents so a reader can trace a claim back to its origin. An official statistic can be reliable while its interpretation still requires scrutiny.</p><h2>What is original at Civora?</h2><p>Civora's initial edition consists of independently written, source-based summaries, explainers, comparisons and analytical interpretations, not eyewitness or interview-based reporting. Original analysis means showing the reasoning between evidence and a conclusion, distinguishing the source's finding from Civora's inference, and making limitations explicit. Restating someone else's press release does not by itself establish new reporting.</p><h2>Statistics and uncertainty</h2><p>For a statistic, we aim to say who counted, what was counted, over which period, and what was excluded or revised. Reported fraud losses are not every loss suffered; a yearly climate figure is not a long-run trend; and internet coverage is not the same as internet use. Derived comparisons should identify their inputs and rounding.</p><h2>Independent judgment and conflicts</h2><p>Advertisers do not direct reporting, and sponsored material must be conspicuously labeled. We do not claim anonymous interviews, access to confidential documents, fieldwork or new measurements that did not occur. Sources and editorial methods should be distinguishable from opinions and assumptions.</p><h2>Accuracy and corrections</h2><p>We correct verified material errors, explain significant changes and preserve a visible dated corrections record. An official newsroom contact method is still pending, and we do not ask readers to send private information through public development channels.</p><h2>AI assistance</h2><p>The first edition was drafted with AI assistance and checked against the primary documents linked in its articles. Generated prose is not evidence. We do not publish invented quotations, sources or events. Where a source does not support a new detail, we omit it or state the limitation.</p><h2>Copyright and imagery</h2><p>Images and other media must be original, public domain or properly licensed. Linking or crediting a copyrighted work does not automatically grant reproduction rights.</p>`,"standards");
simplePage("corrections/index.html","ACCOUNTABILITY","Corrections","Our responsibility continues after an article is published.",`<h2>When an article is wrong</h2><p>We review the underlying evidence, correct verified errors and disclose significant corrections with a date and explanation. Corrections should not quietly erase meaningful mistakes from the record.</p><h2>Corrections log</h2><p>No material corrections had been logged for the first source-based edition as of November 9, 2026. Subsequent significant corrections will be recorded with dates and explanations rather than silently hidden.</p><p>Readers will be able to submit corrections once the official newsroom contact address is configured.</p>`,"corrections");
simplePage("privacy/index.html","TRANSPARENCY","Privacy","Reader preferences, advertising services, and your privacy choices.",`<p><strong>Updated November 9, 2026.</strong> This page explains data used by Civora's public reading experience and third-party services. It does not imply that Google has approved this site for advertising.</p><h2>Reader preferences stored on this device</h2><p>Civora does not currently offer public reader accounts or an active newsletter subscriber database. On-device storage may hold your light/dark theme, saved article identifiers, and recently opened article identifiers. Archive search runs in the browser, although your search words may appear in the URL when you submit it. Civora does not upload the locally saved reading list or history as a reader profile.</p><p><button type="button" class="button-light dark-button" data-clear-reading>Clear saved stories and reading history</button></p><p role="status" aria-live="polite" data-clear-reading-status>Clearing this information affects this device only; it does not delete third-party advertising cookies or hosting logs.</p><h2>Advertising and cookies</h2><p>Civora embeds Google AdSense code under publisher ID ca-pub-1423460909106679. Third-party vendors, including Google, may use cookies and similar identifiers to serve advertisements based on earlier visits to Civora and other websites. Google and its advertising partners may use visit, device and browser information for ad delivery, measurement and, where permitted, personalization. Google may receive technical request data such as an IP address when its scripts load, even if no visible ad is filled. Actual advertising depends on approval, eligibility, browser settings, and regional consent requirements.</p><p>You can control or opt out of personalized Google ads using <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google My Ad Center</a>. For some other participating ad vendors, visit <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">YourAdChoices</a>. These controls may not eliminate all ads, and browser privacy controls or extensions may also limit cookies. Read <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's advertising privacy information</a> for details.</p><h2>Consent and regional choices</h2><p>Where law requires consent, including relevant European advertising requirements, an appropriate certified consent-management platform and regional choices must be configured through the advertising provider. A privacy-policy link alone is not consent. The presence of the AdSense script does not prove that a consent message is active or that the site has been approved. Readers should be able to use the editorial pages whether or not an ad is filled.</p><h2>Hosting and content delivery</h2><p>GitHub Pages hosts Civora's static pages and may process technical request information through its hosting systems. Google Fonts is requested for typography and may receive device/network request information. Parts of the live news feed and dynamic story reader request public content from Supabase; those network services may process technical connection information. Those requests are distinct from Civora's on-device saved-story and reading-history features. External source links lead to sites with their own privacy practices.</p><h2>Newsroom and policy changes</h2><p>Staff publishing tools use separate restricted access and are not public reader accounts. We will revise this disclosure if the site's collection, subscriptions, analytics, advertising vendors or consent setup changes. For publication and correction availability, see the <a href="../contact/">Contact</a> and <a href="../corrections/">Corrections</a> pages; no private tip-submission channel is currently offered.</p>`,"privacy");
simplePage("advertise/index.html","PARTNER WITH CIVORA","Advertising","Advertising information and editorial independence.",`<div class="policy-callout"><strong>AdSense integration added.</strong><p>Civora has installed Google AdSense verification and automatic-ad code. Showing ads and earning revenue depend on account approval and configuration; we do not claim approval, paid impressions or guaranteed reach. Direct sponsorship placements are not currently offered.</p></div><h2>Our principles</h2><p>Advertisements must remain distinguishable from editorial reporting. No advertiser can purchase favorable news coverage or influence fact-checking conclusions.</p><p>Information about independent sponsorship opportunities will be published if direct advertising sales become available.</p>`,"advertise");
simplePage("contact/index.html","GET IN TOUCH","Contact","Newsroom contact details will be announced when an official mailbox is configured.",`<h2>For now</h2><p>There is no public newsroom inbox or anonymous tip system. Please do not send confidential sources, sensitive details or personal data through public GitHub issues.</p><h2>Corrections and feedback</h2><p>An official contact method and privacy-aware corrections process will be introduced before expanding reporting operations.</p>`,"contact");
